  <relations type="MAY_CAUSE" sourceType="Drug" sourceId="glyburide-and-metformin" targetType="Condition" targetId="lactic-acidosis" confidence="0.85" evidence="Drug interactions— The concomitant use of glyburide and metformin hydrochloride with specific drugs may increase the risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis: those that impair renal function, result in significant hemodynamic change, interfere with acid-base balance, or increase metformin accumulation [ see Drug Interactions ( 7 ) ] ." sourceSpanStart="7989" sourceSpanEnd="8330" chunkIndex="4"/>
